---
title: Local browser origin and private API network
query: >-
  Describe the implemented default local network only. Browser React assets,
  raw uploads and offline Redoc all use one loopback frontend origin. Compose
  publishes 127.0.0.1:FRONTEND_PORT to NGINX container port 8080; the default
  host port is 8080 and the recorded operator choice is 18084. NGINX forwards
  uploads and docs to api:3000 over the private Compose network. The normal API
  has expose only, with no host-published port. Exactly two runtime containers
  start without a cloud dependency. Show the independent host Playwright and
  controller separately against isolated test containers, with temporary
  test-only loopback API diagnostics. Never imply this diagnostic port exists
  in normal Compose or that tests are a third application container.
references:
  - 'File: /compose.yaml'
  - 'File: /Makefile'
  - 'File: /frontend/nginx.conf.template'
  - 'File: /frontend/Dockerfile'
  - 'File: /server/Dockerfile'
  - 'File: /server/src/http/config.ts'
  - 'File: /server/src/docs.ts'
  - 'File: /scripts/run-e2e.mjs'
  - 'File: /scripts/e2e-controller.mjs'
